DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/pediatric-palliative-care-in-
 africa-research-partnerships-and-quality-of-life\n報名/票券: https://f
 orms.gle/jbhbHezx4ChfMLkg6\n\nSession Description:\n\nThis presentation wi
 ll explore the role of pediatric palliative care in improving quality of l
 ife for children with serious illness and their families across Africa. Dr
 . Justin Baker will introduce the field and its growing importance within 
 global child health. Dr. Claire Wakefield will discuss the work of the Qua
 lity of Life for All (QoLA) Lab at Stanford Medicine and its emerging rese
 arch partnerships in sub-Saharan Africa focused on understanding and impro
 ving quality of life outcomes for children and families. Dr. Eve Namisango
 \, Executive Director of the African Palliative Care Association (APCA)\, 
 will share perspectives on palliative care development across the continen
 t and highlight her current research and capacity-building initiatives.\n\
 nSpeakers' bio:\n\nJustin Baker is Chief of the Division of Quality of Lif
 e and Pediatric Palliative Care at Stanford Medicine Children's Health and
  an Endowed Professor at Stanford University. An internationally recognize
 d leader in pediatric palliative care\, his work focuses on improving qual
 ity of life\, communication\, and care for children with serious illness a
 nd their families. He serves as Chair of the Board of the International Ch
 ildren's Palliative Care Network and has worked extensively to advance ped
 iatric palliative care education\, research\, and access around the world\
 , including across Africa.\n \nClaire E. Wakefield is Director of Research
  for the Division of Quality of Life and Pediatric Palliative Care
